Z||000001||Mach10||11-06-2001||10:08 PM||||So which do you want? Dual suspension, or a Good Bike?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Not a fan of dualies... Gimme a nice light set of Judy's up front, and a stiff, light chromoly frame... Less crap to break, and easier to ride.<P>Sorry, I'm not much help, am I  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000002||Flamberge||11-06-2001||10:17 PM||||I agree with Mach10...to a degree. I have a hardtail (front suspension only) GT that I love. Ful suspension is generally overkill, and makes it harder to climb hills, since they bounce as you try to petal, absorbing your energy.<P>However, GT (used to) make the LTS-1,2,3,etc which were very nice.<BR><P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroFanaticus2||11-06-2001||10:32 PM||||Hey, I've got a RedLine ProLine 2 that I used to ride.  It's not a mountain bike, but it only weighs 11 pounds.  Modified for street racing -- No brakes.  Fast! (For a single speed bike anyway).||||reg||1
